**Khaos** was one of the two war alliances born from [[the-great-collapse|The Great Collapse]] of 11 May 2021, formed largely from the core of [[Goose]].{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} It fought the ex-[[Valhalla]] guilds for a year and was defunct by 26 June 2022, its guilds absorbed into [[Cucumber Company]].{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}

## History

### Founding
On 11 May 2021 Goose and [[Artemis]] collapsed on the same day. While thirteen guilds formed Valhalla, nine formed Khaos: [[Aequitas]], Wheres The Finish, Nerfuria, Tartarus Wrath, Ultra Violet, Fuzzy Spiders, ChinaNumberOne, Cyphrus Code and Eden — most of them the bloc that had joined Goose in its final spring.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} Tartarus Wrath was created days after the founding and joined mid-May; Cyphrus Code's stint lasted only until late May, an end inferred from its last territory exchange.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

The name itself barely survives in writing: a single megalist post of 25 May 2021 records that “the two major alliances both disbanded and got new names… Valhalla and Kaos”.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|post #136, Dream, 25 May 2021}} No public Khaos roster was ever posted — by then alliance rosters lived in a Google Sheet never captured by any archive — and the membership derives from the community Timeline document.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

### The war with Valhalla and Vanir
The [[valhalla-khaos-war|Valhalla-Khaos war]] began the day both blocs formed and outlasted Valhalla itself, with [[Vanir]] inheriting the opposing side.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} TheNoLifes — excluded from Vanir after turning on its Valhalla allies — joined Khaos around December 2021: testimony names it among Khaos's leaders{{cite:oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}}, and map data shows it erupting against the ex-Valhalla guilds that month.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The war peaked in January 2022 at 500–800 quiet-territory exchanges per week{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} against an opposing coalition remembered in testimony as “the Pineapple Pact” (a name with no surviving written record){{cite:oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}}, then faded through the spring.

### End
No dissolution was ever announced; the end is a documentary bound. Fighting faded to nothing by mid-July 2022{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}, and when the fourteen-guild Cucumber Company roster was posted to the megalist on 26 June 2022 — explicitly replacing the old alliance listing as incorrect — Khaos was gone, with several of its guilds, Aequitas among them, inside the new bloc.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Khaos}}

## Legacy
Khaos was the last opponent of the Valhalla line, and its fade set up the [[the-realignment-era|2022 realignment]]: within months its guilds and their former enemies were trading territory as allies inside Cucumber Company.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #160, TherapueticLiz, 26 Jun 2022}}

**Luna** was a Wynncraft war alliance of 2019, formed on 14 Feb 2019 to counter [[SOL]].{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} In five months it went from a counter-bloc to sole master of the territory map — wiping every guild but [[Avicia]] in July — before a leadership revolt and the rise of [[Terra]] destroyed it in September. Its rise and fall form the centrepiece of [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the Alliance Wars of 2019]].

## History

### Formation
Luna was formed on 14 Feb 2019 by [[Imperial]], [[Emorians]], Blacklisted, BuildCraftia and others, explicitly to counter SOL, the bloc left standing after [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s fall.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} The founding list in the community Timeline document is marked as a placeholder, and the record contradicts part of it: contrary to some retellings, exchange data shows [[Kingdom Foxes]] was not a founding member — Luna was at war with Fox from its second day.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### The war on Kingdom Foxes
From 15 Feb 2019 Luna fought Kingdom Foxes across more than 300 territories; Imperial alone attacked Fox 660 times.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The war ended when Fox joined Luna on 8 Jul 2019 — the day after the Treaty of Ternaves, in which Fox, [[The Simple Ones]] and ThisIsMurica divided the territory of the dissolved Celestial Tigers.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

### Full map control
After fending off an attack on Kingdom Foxes in July 2019, Luna wiped every guild on the map except Avicia; Avicia joined on 17 Jul 2019, and Luna held the entire map.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

{{map:2019-07-17|Luna at full map control}}

### Luna as the Valkyrie bloc
A participant on the opposing side framed it differently. In a memoir chapter published on 14 Sep 2019 — a recollection, but written while the war was still being fought — [[arkada|Arkada]] of [[Titans Valor]] describes not a new alliance but a renaming: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians" broke a summer raid on Kingdom Foxes, took the map in under two days, and thereafter appears in his account as "the Valkyrie alliance, now calling themselves the Luna alliance".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” to “ASSAULTS ON BCR”, 14 Sep 2019}} He blames the raid's failure on Valkyrie's "controversial use of sub guilds", by which main-guild members "could defend land more quickly by branching into sub guilds", and names Blacklisted and BuildCraftia as the first defectors, followed by Avicia and The Simple Ones.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID” and “THE FORMATION OF LUNA”, 14 Sep 2019}}

The framing supports the chronicle's position that the [[Valkyrie]] network "warred publicly as Luna in 2019"{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}, but it does not fit the recorded dates: the chronicle dates Luna's founding to February 2019 against SOL, while Arkada places the bloc's emergence after the midsummer raid and treats Imperial and [[Paladins United]] as long-standing Valkyrie members although their recorded Valkyrie membership begins only in September 2019 — with this memoir as its first attestation.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} The discrepancy is set out on the [[imperial|Imperial]] and Paladins United pages.

### Revolt and collapse
On 29 Aug 2019, after a leadership dispute, Emorians and Avicia left Luna and declared war on Imperial, spiralling into a large war over Gavel; ThisIsMurica was kicked the next day for sending fighters, and Terra formed in the chaos on 30 Aug.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} Arkada adds a cause for the Emorians' turn from neutral exile to belligerent: Luna "seized all of its lands" after the departure, which he judged "a large mistake", since it made the Emorians sympathetic to the resistance.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“A RAY OF HOPE”, 14 Sep 2019}} In the Luna–Terra war of 7–19 Sep 2019, The Simple Ones defected to Terra on 8 Sep and Terra took map control the same day{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} — over 2,000 exchanges swept across 322 territories in ten days.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} A week of Luna counter-raids failed, and on 14 Sep 2019 Luna mounted an organised counter-raid that Terra had been warned of by a spy: "In the morning, Luna struck, but we struck harder. In the late afternoon, Luna struck again, but we struck even harder." That action is recorded only in Arkada's memoir, written the same day.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“LUNA'S RETALIATION”, 14 Sep 2019}} Kingdom Foxes left on the 18th, and Luna collapsed.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

## Membership
At its July–August 2019 peak the chronicle records ten member guilds at once.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

{{alliance:Luna}}

## Legacy
Luna's fall handed the map to Terra, whose core went on to found the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]]. The chronicle's Valkyrie record adds a longer perspective: the long-running Valkyrie network "warred publicly as Luna in 2019"{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} — Luna serving as the war-fighting face of a much older community alliance.

**Niflheim** was a community alliance of 2020–2021 that ran alongside — and overlapped with — the war blocs of its day. Its four attested members were simultaneously war-alliance guilds, and it dissolved on 18 December 2021, the same day [[Vanir]] collapsed.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

## History
Niflheim's formation was never documented. Its first dated record is [[ShadowFall]]'s join on 27 December 2020.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} The only attested roster is a megalist post of 7 July 2021 naming the “Niflheim community alliance” as [[Avicia]], Blue Nations United [IBT] (the guild known today as IceBlue Team), ShadowFall and TheNoLifes; the three joins other than ShadowFall's are therefore “by” dates.{{cite:thread-278112-p08|post #146, HungHung, 7 Jul 2021}}

All four members belonged to war alliances at the same time — attested in [[Goose]] by February 2021, with three of the four going on to found [[Valhalla]] in May{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} — illustrating the era's layering of community alliances over war blocs. Niflheim itself has no recorded part in any war, and by 2021 the map is so saturated with allied territory-trading that no distinct Niflheim signal can be separated from the surrounding blocs.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

Niflheim was officially dissolved on 18 December 2021 — the same day Vanir collapsed.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

## Membership
{{alliance:Niflheim}}

## Legacy
Alongside [[Hestia]] and the [[Empire of Nemract]], Niflheim is one of the few community alliances of the era with an attested roster{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} — a reminder that beneath the war-alliance churn of 2020–2021 ran a quieter, more stable social layer.

**Seraphim**, styled the Seraphim Alliance, was a community alliance of August 2016 founded by the player Dacleos. It is notable less for what it did than for what it declined to do: it was formed in the middle of [[hackforums|HackForums]]' map dominance and defined itself by refusing to fight, and its thread became the venue for the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]]'s most substantive surviving argument about that dominance.

## History

The thread opened on 8 August 2016 with an unusually candid statement of purpose. "Do you like guild wars? Do you like dominating the territory map and controlling the entire province of Wynn...? Well get the fuck out then," the opening post began, before setting out the terms: "The Seraphim alliance is a 100% community based alliance... There's no intention of actively providing support for guild wars."{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}} What it offered instead was a way around the guild-slot cap of the period — "an opportunity to grow their communities beyond the bugged-out, limited guild slots" — plus shared art and thread graphics, and the founder was frank about his motive: "80% of the reason I set this up is because I want an excuse to make new graphics." Membership was deliberately non-exclusive: "any guild can join the alliance, regardless of if they are already in another alliance."{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}}

Within a day the thread was taken over by an argument between veterans about whether HackForums' position resembled [[ordo-malleus|Ordo Malleus]]' earlier control of the map. That exchange — Glitchedslayer against [[drew1011|Drew1011]], LeoDiesAlot and Yuno F Gasai — is now the principal source for Ordo Malleus, for Hax's ejection from it, and for the composition of the bloc holding territory in 2016{{cite:thread-143392|posts #7–#15, 9 Aug 2016}}, in which LeoDiesAlot noted that Hax "work with Lir and Bla in order to hold territories".{{cite:thread-143392|post #12, LeoDiesAlot, 9 Aug 2016}} The founder's own verdict on his thread: "Thanks for hijacking my thread gais. Appreciate it."{{cite:thread-143392|post #16, 9 Aug 2016}}

## Membership

Four member guilds are attested in the opening post's roster graphics: Saltiest, [[libertas|Libertas]], FOX and Holders Of LE.{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening-post roster graphics}} The inclusion of Libertas is the striking one — on the API leaderboard capture of 23 September 2016, six weeks later, Libertas held 60 territories, second only to HackForums' 146{{cite:Wayback Machine capture of the api.wynncraft.com guild leaderboard, 23 Sep 2016 (pre-2018 territory snapshots)}}, so a declared community alliance with no war function counted among its members the map's second-largest warring power. Holders Of LE was simultaneously a member of [[halcyon|Halcyon]]{{cite:thread-130444|post #1, opening post (Halcyon founded 5 Jun 2016 between ToastedPandas and Holders of LE)}} and joined [[valkyrie|Valkyrie]] that October{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}}, which the alliance's own rules expressly permitted.{{cite:thread-143392|post #1, opening post (thread opened 8 Aug 2016; OP last revised 20 Aug 2016)}}

Seraphim predates the machine-recorded chronicle, which begins in January 2018, so no live membership card exists for it.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

## Legacy

No source records Seraphim doing anything after its founding, and none records its end. What it preserved was the argument it hosted: nearly everything the record retains about Ordo Malleus, and the clearest contemporaneous statement that HackForums was not acting alone, survive because they were written on the thread of an alliance that was set up as a joke about not warring.{{cite:thread-143392|posts #7–#15, 9 Aug 2016}}

**smtn elf** was the final name of the merged super-alliance that dominated Wynncraft warring in 2022–23: [[Cucumber Company]] renamed “Smtn else” at the start of guild Season 8 in autumn 2022, then renamed again to “smtn elf” for Christmas 2022 — and never changed back. It fell apart in June 2023 when [[The Aquarium]] and [[Avicia]] walked out.

## History

### From Cucumber to elf
Per [[titan-times|Titan Times]] vol. 6 (12 October 2022), at the start of Season 8 “Cucumber was archived. The new alliance name is called Smtn else” — the same issue records Gang of Fools having “left and betrayed the alliance” and welcomes [[Paladins United]], [[The Simple Ones]] and TerraLune.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol6|vol. 6, 12 Oct 2022}}{{cite:“SMTN ELSE SLANDER”, video by TherapueticLiz, 3 Oct 2022}} The Christmas 2022 rename to “smtn elf” rests on oral-history testimony{{cite:oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}}, corroborated by the name appearing in writing by 17 February 2023 — in a forum thread that dubbed it “unquestionably the greatest super-alliance of 2023” (a tongue-in-cheek thread, but the name and the bloc's scale were real).{{cite:https://forums.wynncraft.com/threads/306790/|Wynncraft forums thread 306790, 17 Feb 2023}} Because the sources frame Season 8 as a rename rather than a reformation, the chronicle carries the full Cucumber roster through it{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}; only part of that roster is individually re-attested in the smtn-else era.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol8|vol. 8}}

### 2023
Titan Times vol. 9 (25 March 2023) records the mid-season changes: busted moments joined (a brief stint, over by the end of May), Nefarious Ravens left “on account of the guild disbanding” — its last map exchange was 9 March 2023{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} — and [[Idiot Co]], which joined that spring, held alliance territory.{{cite:titantimes-github-io-vol9|vol. 9, 25 Mar 2023}}

### The end
In June 2023 The Aquarium and Avicia quit, rejecting pressure — led by busted moments, per testimony — to shrink their territorial claims: [[the-avocado-split|the Avocado split]].{{cite:oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}} The alliance's last recorded mention is Avicia's Season 12 post of 10 June 2023 (“To our other allies in smtn elf... thank you for the hqs”){{cite:https://forums.wynncraft.com/threads/308780/|Avicia Season 12 post, Wynncraft forums thread 308780, 10 Jun 2023}}; by the Season 13 post of 19 August 2023 it had vanished from the record entirely.{{cite:https://forums.wynncraft.com/threads/310286/|Avicia Season 13 post, Wynncraft forums thread 310286, 19 Aug 2023}} No death announcement exists, and map data shows the remaining guilds never fought each other — smtn elf did not break up so much as quietly cease to be.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

## Membership
The roster is carried over from Cucumber Company at the Season 8 rename, with the changes attested in Titan Times; joins are approximated to the season boundary.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

{{alliance:smtn elf}}

## Legacy
smtn elf was the last of the public super-alliances, and its unannounced death is the [[private-diplomacy-era|private-diplomacy era]] in miniature: no roster, no dissolution notice, just silence between two season posts. Its collapse set up the [[Avocado Aquarium]] pact and the wars that followed.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

**SOL** was the Wynncraft war alliance born from [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s ashes in late 2018 — a leading power of the winter interregnum and the bloc [[Luna]] was explicitly formed to counter. It is also among the least documented major alliances: no written roster of SOL exists anywhere.

## History

### Creation
SOL was created in the post-collapse chaos following the Federation's fall of 10 Nov 2018; the community timeline records only that "SOL was created at this time."{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} The chronicle approximates its start to about December 2018.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The war with Luna
On 14 Feb 2019, Luna was formed "as an alliance to counter SOL," and the two blocs fought through the spring as part of [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the Alliance Wars of 2019]].{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} SOL was still described as a current bloc in June 2019 — "the current SOL and Luna guilds"{{cite:thread-251543|post #1, Pikacal, 26 Jun 2019}} — and then vanishes from the record as Luna consolidated the map in July. No dissolution was ever recorded; June 2019 is simply its last attestation.

### The inferred roster
No member list of SOL was ever written down. The chronicle's six-guild roster — [[DiamondDeities]], Achte Shadow, Wrath Of Poseidon, Beyond the Scene, Spectral Cabbage, and from January 2019 Ecliptic Awakening — is inferred from map data: these guilds fought Luna's founders from Luna's founding onward across quiet (non-free-for-all) territories, Beyond the Scene alone accounting for nearly 4,000 quiet-territory exchanges, while showing near-zero fighting among themselves.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} The chronicle treats this roster as medium confidence.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} DiamondDeities' membership is consistent with the Treaty of Rodoroc — its peace with [[Kingdom Foxes]], effective 2 Mar 2019{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} — and with a late-2018 arrangement to share Molten Heights with Fox recorded on the community timeline.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

## Membership
{{alliance:SOL}}

## Legacy
SOL bridged the Federation's fall and the alliance wars that consumed 2019: it inherited the map's chaos, provoked Luna into existence, and dissolved into obscurity without a recorded ending. Several of its inferred members resurfaced in the autumn blocs — DiamondDeities and Achte Shadow both appear in [[Terra]].{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

**Terra** was a short-lived Wynncraft war alliance of autumn 2019 — the bloc that broke [[Luna]]'s total map control. Formed on 30 Aug 2019 and fallen by 2 Nov, it held the map for under two months, and its core went on to found the [[Council of Canyon Kingdoms]].

## History

### Formation
Terra formed on 30 Aug 2019 in opposition to Luna, amid the Emorians–Avicia revolt that had broken out the day before{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}; several of its guilds were already fighting Luna from 25 Aug.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

A participant account describes it as a merger rather than a founding. In a memoir chapter published on 14 Sep 2019 — a recollection, but written mid-war — [[arkada|Arkada]] of [[Titans Valor]] records that after Luna took the map his guild joined **The Ascendancy**, "a small and weak band of guilds that resisted Luna through unsuccessful attacks", and that as more guilds tired of Luna's reign, "small alliances similar to The Ascendancy merged together, forming a larger and more organized counter-alliance called Terra".{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“ASSAULTS ON BCR” and “A RAY OF HOPE”, 14 Sep 2019}} By the time of the decisive raid the merged bloc fielded "nearly 15 guilds"{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE WEEKEND RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} — more than the twelve the chronicle records{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}, which is consistent with a roster that was never published. The Ascendancy outlived Terra as a distinct grouping: its departure collapsed the Council of Canyon Kingdoms on 23 Nov 2019.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### The Luna–Terra war
The war for the map ran 7–19 Sep 2019: over 2,000 attacks across 322 territories in ten days — a genuine full-map war, with only 37% of the fighting on the usual free-for-all hotspots.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} [[The Simple Ones]] defected from Luna to Terra on 8 Sep, and Terra took map control the same day; [[Kingdom Foxes]] left Luna on the 18th and Luna collapsed.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} Arkada's memoir describes the decisive action as a weekend raid intended only to take [[Imperial]]'s land, which instead "ended in nearly six hours and resulted in the complete wipe of all Luna guilds except Kingdom Foxes"{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE WEEKEND RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}}, followed on 14 Sep by a Luna counter-raid that Terra repelled.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“LUNA'S RETALIATION”, 14 Sep 2019}}

{{map:2019-09-08|The map as Terra took control}}

### Dispersal and fall
A week after victory, on 15 Sep 2019, Terra's core — Kingdom Foxes, [[DiamondDeities]], Titans Valor, The Simple Ones, [[Fantasy]], Phantom Hearts and Empire of Sindria — founded the Council of Canyon Kingdoms.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} [[Paladins United]] departed at [[Artemis]]'s founding on 30 Oct.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} Terra itself fell on 2 Nov 2019, seven weeks after taking the map; on 10 Nov its fragments launched one final raid on the newborn Artemis.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

## Membership
Terra's roster is largely map-inferred: the Timeline document's founding roster is literally a placeholder{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}, and only The Simple Ones' membership is documented (it joined hours after leaving Luna). The other recorded members are the guilds that mounted 100 or more attacks on Luna during the decisive September war window.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

{{alliance:Terra}}

## Legacy
Terra ended the last period of single-alliance map control in 2019 and seeded what came next: its core formed the Council of Canyon Kingdoms, and Paladins United left it to co-found Artemis, the alliance that would anchor the following era.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

The **Federation** (tag **Fed**) was the dominant war alliance of 2018 on Wynncraft — the largest alliance the game had yet seen, holding the entire territory map for eight months and twenty-five days before collapsing in a single day on 10 Nov 2018. Founded and unofficially led by [[Drew1011]], it grew to 37–40 member guilds and gave its name to the [[federation-era|Federation era]].{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

## History

### Formation
The Federation was born from the fracture of the [[Coalition]]. Around 16 Feb 2018, five guilds left the Coalition over map disputes and formed [[Alliance Alliance]]; the Coalition remnant merged with the remains of War Syndicate — the power the Coalition had wiped the previous Christmas — into a new alliance, founded and led by Drew1011.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} Even its genealogy was disputed among participants: a 2020 retrospective describes the Coa–WS merger as "a creation of fed"{{cite:thread-265297|post #16, Lego_DW, 4 Apr 2020}}, while Slayne posted a rival claim on the tribute thread on 14 Nov 2018 — "In a way, you could say that I created Fed because I (along with some others) created Double AA. Take that drew! Owait. Im also drew."{{cite:thread-237070-p03|post #45, Slayne, 14 Nov 2018}} The claim is causal rather than direct: "Double AA" is Alliance Alliance, whose split from the Coalition triggered the merger that produced the Federation.

### Governance
The alliance ran on a Discord server built by AurumKitsune of KingdomPhoenixes, who in Drew1011's tribute is thanked "for setting up the discord and coming up with things such as the 2/3 majority voting rule that contributed greatly to its success".{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} That two-thirds majority is the only decision rule recorded for the bloc anywhere in the corpus; how it was applied in practice, and to what class of decisions, was never written down.

### The wipe of HackForums
On 19 Feb 2018, three days after forming, the Federation attacked [[HackForums]]' 111 territories and [[the-wipe-of-hackforums|wiped them to zero]] in under 12 hours{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} — the end of Hax as a territorial power, a year after its 2017 peak of roughly 350 territories.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}

### Map dominance
The Federation took full map control on 20 Mar 2018, ending the [[coalition-civil-war|Coalition Civil War]] and absorbing the Alliance Alliance guilds.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} By its founder's account it held the entire map for 8 months and 25 days, with a roughly three-day interruption in March.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} An archived guild-leaderboard capture of 16 Apr 2018 shows all fifteen territory holders on the map were Federation guilds, together holding 384 territories.{{cite:Wayback Machine guild-leaderboard API capture, 16 Apr 2018 (pre-2018 territory snapshots)}}

{{map:2018-04-16|The Federation's map at its height}}

The bloc's fighting core is named once in the record: replying to the tribute on 13 Nov 2018, the member Lego_DW asked for recognition of "the absolute gods of war this alliance created" — himself, 21(n), Goden, _Antho74_, InnerJoker, 0x7cf and snowy — who "along with too many others to credit, were the ones that really held the alliance together in terms of war power".{{cite:thread-237070|post #18, Lego_DW, 13 Nov 2018}} Only Goden, a [[kingdom-foxes|Kingdom Foxes]] officer, is otherwise placed in the corpus; the others appear nowhere else.

Membership churned heavily — [[Titans Valor]] alone served three separate stints.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} Within the bloc, [[Fantasy]], Sins of Seedia and IceBlue Team formed the [[Aesir Pact]] on 25 Mar 2018{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}, a pact of sister guilds dedicated to Gavel.{{cite:thread-227373|post #1, opening post (lotuss/simplyinfinity_)}} Fantasy itself left the Federation in late May 2018 — a departure recorded nowhere in writing, but map-data analysis shows off-FFA fighting jumping to sustained war levels in the week of 28 May — and fought the bloc across more than 220 territories all summer before rejoining on 29 Oct 2018.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

### Collapse
At around 3 AM EST on 10 Nov 2018, one guild left the Federation — and the alliance cascaded apart within a day.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} The sequence of [[the-federation-dies|the Federation's death]] was recorded by members days later: The Hive had left a month earlier, then Odysseia; [[Imperial]]'s exit for independence "snowballed into a major attack on Fed together with the enemy alliance [Ent]"; Arisen followed, and after 14 hours of constant warring the Aesir Pact guilds quit, ending it.{{cite:thread-236962|post #17, Ascended Kitten, 11 Nov 2018}} The tag **[Ent]** is the only identifier ever given for the opposing bloc, and it matches no alliance recorded elsewhere in the corpus; who fought under it on 10 Nov 2018 is unresolved. "What killed Federation was... internal affairs," wrote Drew1011 in his tribute, posted three days later with the full member roster.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}}

## Membership
The founder's tribute names 37 member guilds (one of them, "Death Reapers", resolves to no known guild in the prefix record); with renames and re-joins the chronicle records the alliance at 37–40 guilds.{{cite:thread-237070|post #1, Drew1011, 13 Nov 2018}} Rename chains within the roster — LE Flowers → [[DiamondDeities]], DogsAmongUs → White Lotus, As Darkness Falls → Constellations — are verified by abutting activity windows in the exchange data.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}}

{{alliance:Federation}}

## Legacy
The Federation's fall ended 2018's era of single-bloc dominance and opened a winter interregnum in which, per the community timeline, "all guilds keep to themselves with valk owning most of Gavel" — the quiet territorial peak of the [[Valkyrie]] network.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} [[SOL]] was created in the post-collapse chaos{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}}, and [[Luna]] was formed to counter it in February 2019, beginning [[the-alliance-wars-of-2019|the Alliance Wars of 2019]].{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} No later alliance matched the Federation's documented duration of total map control.

**Valhalla** was the dominant war alliance of mid-to-late 2021, formed on 11 May 2021 by thirteen guilds — including [[The Aquarium]] — out of the simultaneous collapse of [[Goose]] and [[Artemis]]. It took map control within days and held it until its members reorganized as [[Vanir]] on 28 November 2021.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}}

## History

### Founding
On 11 May 2021, in [[the-great-collapse|The Great Collapse]], Goose and Artemis dissolved on the same day. Thirteen guilds — drawn from Goose's broad membership together with Artemis alumni such as [[Titans Valor]] — formed Valhalla, with Guardian of Wynn joining immediately after the founding.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} A megalist post of 25 May 2021 corroborates the reorganization: “the two major alliances both disbanded and got new names… Valhalla and Kaos”.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|post #136, Dream, 25 May 2021}} No public roster was ever posted — the megalist's alliance rosters lived in a Google Sheet never captured by any archive — and the chronicle's membership derives from the community Timeline document.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} This is the first alliance membership recorded for The Aquarium in the chronicle.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

### Dominance
Valhalla took map control from Goose's remnants in mid-May 2021 and dominated for the rest of the year while fighting the [[valhalla-khaos-war|Valhalla-Khaos war]].{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} A forum thread of 25 September 2021 captures its standing: “the meta of being top 10 on the guild sr leaderboard is to join valhalla”.{{cite:thread-295680|post #1, IamFye, 25 Sep 2021}}

### Betrayal and reorganization
Friction with two members, The Mage Legacy and TheNoLifes, is visible in map data from August 2021. Both turned openly on their allies — December 2021 saw 5,359 quiet-territory exchanges as the fighting erupted{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} — and when ten Valhalla guilds reorganized as Vanir on 28 November 2021, both were excluded.{{cite:community Timeline document (chronicle research corpus)}} Per testimony, TheNoLifes went on to help lead [[Khaos]].{{cite:oral-history testimony (Cameron, TAq veteran)}} No formal Valhalla dissolution was ever recorded; its end date is inferred from Vanir's founding.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

