## Legacy
Valhalla headed the alliance line that ran Goose–Valhalla–Vanir and, after the winter war with Khaos, fed the [[the-realignment-era|2022 realignment]] into [[Cucumber Company]].{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} Its era also marks the closing of the public record: it was the first dominant alliance whose roster never appeared in public.

**Valkyrie** (tag **Valk**) was the longest-lived alliance in Wynncraft history, running continuously from its founding on 2 Jun 2015 to its last attestation on 19 Sep 2022. Founded by Kingdom of Foxes (later [[Kingdom Foxes]]) and [[Imperial]] "not for the purpose of war" and governed by an Electorate of guild masters{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}}, it persisted as a social and political layer beneath — and once, briefly, above — every war bloc from the [[early-guild-era|early guild era]] to the eve of [[the-realignment-era|the realignment era]].

## History

### Founding and the Electorate (2015)
Valkyrie's founding thread was opened on 10 Sep 2015 by [[lovelusting|LoveLusting]], "Queen of the Foxes", and set out both the date and the purpose: "It was initially founded between the Kingdom of Foxes and Imperial, and unlike many other alliances, Valkyrie was not established for the purpose of war. Rather, the partnership was created with the aim of solidifying and maintaining the already very good social relations between the two guilds. The agreement was formally put into action on June 2, 2015, in honour of the Kingdom of Foxes' 1-year anniversary."{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}}

Its constitution left internal government alone and pooled only foreign policy: "While guild governments may still maintain their powers with regards to their respective internal affairs, all powers regarding the conclusion of foreign affairs or policy will be forfeited to the Valkyrie Electorate. This administration comprises the guild leaders of each member-guild and functions using unanimous agreement in their decision-making process."{{cite:thread-89529|post #1, opening post (thread opened 10 Sep 2015)}} A third guild followed that winter: at a joint award ceremony on 12 Dec 2015, LoveLusting announced that "the Lightly Toasted Heroes, lead by klove and Emily, will be joining the Valkyrie Alliance."{{cite:thread-89529|post #16, LoveLusting, 7 Jan 2016 (reporting the ceremony of 12 Dec 2015)}}

### The Parliament and the 2016 relaunches
Valkyrie's thread was rebuilt twice in thirteen months by three different keepers, and the succession was explained in passing by the second of them. "ahri left so Kv had to make a new one, then Kv left so now I run this thing," Yuno F Gasai of Imperial wrote on 13 Sep 2016, giving the chain ahri to Kv to Yuno.{{cite:thread-147790|post #15, Yuno F Gasai, 13 Sep 2016}} Yuno's relaunch thread, opened 29 Aug 2016, reused the founding text with one substitution: the Electorate had become the "Valkyrie Parliament", now "the guild masters of each member-guild", still acting by unanimity. Its roster of four — Imperial, Kingdom of Foxes, House of Sentinels and Lightly Toasted Heroes [Lth] — is the largest concurrent membership attested in any of the alliance's own threads.{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, opening post (thread opened 29 Aug 2016)}} House of Sentinels' presence is confirmed in the thread's own banter, where Yuno answered a rival's boast with "pretzule leads a Valkyrie guild tho".{{cite:thread-147790|post #8, Yuno F Gasai, 29 Aug 2016}}

The third relaunch, opened on 15 Oct 2016 by [[drew1011|Drew1011]], marks the point where the alliance had outlived its founders.{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}} Imperial had left in the intervening weeks — "Hey, we are pretty alive," its leadership replied to a mourner in the thread, "Just not in the alliance anymore"{{cite:thread-159734|post #7, Ascended Kitten, 15 Oct 2016}} — and Lightly Toasted Heroes had also gone, "a few weeks ago"{{cite:thread-159734|post #11, Drew1011, 15 Oct 2016}}, according to Drew1011, "in order to try and revive the guild".{{cite:thread-159734|post #18, Yuno F Gasai, 21 Oct 2016}} The reaction was elegiac: "R.I.P OG Valkyrie guilds", wrote DireFire{{cite:thread-159734|post #5, DireFire, 15 Oct 2016}}, and another reader observed "tmw the alliance originally made by Imp and Fox has neither Imp nor Fox in it"{{cite:thread-159734|post #2, Zahr, 15 Oct 2016}} — a remark that sits awkwardly beside the relaunch roster of Kingdom of Foxes, Holders of LE and Ha Ha United{{cite:thread-159734|post #1, opening post (thread opened 15 Oct 2016)}}, and beside the community timeline's claim that Kingdom of Foxes had disbanded on 2 Jul 2016 and was not revived until 3 Dec 2016.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Whether Fox was a real member or a nominal one in October 2016 is unresolved; both readings are recorded here. Drew1011's forum profile dates his leadership precisely to that thread: "Leader of Valkyrie Alliance: 15 October 2016 — 10 March 2018".{{cite:Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile title chain}}

### The Federation years (2018)
Valkyrie persisted through the year of [[the-federation|the Federation]]'s total map dominance, several of its members simultaneously inside the war bloc. The Hive joined around March 2018 (welcomed that April as having "joined a month prior"), and [[Emorians]] joined on 23 May 2018.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} The stints of Holders Of LE and HaHaUnited are approximated as ending at a leadership restructure on 10 Mar 2018 — the day Drew1011's Valkyrie leadership title ends{{cite:Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile title chain}} — after which neither is re-attested.

### The interregnum (winter 2018–19)
After [[the-federation-dies|the Federation died]] in November 2018, the community timeline records that "all guilds keep to themselves with valk owning most of Gavel" — the closest the alliance ever came to territorial power in its own name.{{cite:thread-265297|post #1, the community guild-timeline image (imgur seklYAQ)}} Exchange data corroborates it: Kingdom Foxes and Imperial were the interregnum's top territory gainers.{{cite:territory_exchanges map-data analysis}} Drew1011's Valkyrie officer titles run through Jan 2019.{{cite:Drew1011's Wynncraft forum profile title chain}}

### Luna and after (2019)
In 2019 the bloc warred publicly as [[Luna]], with Valkyrie remaining the social layer beneath the war alliance — the chronicle resolves the apparent Fox-versus-Imperial fighting of that spring this way, as a war fought under Luna's banner.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}} Emorians' Valkyrie stint ends with its August 2019 Luna exit. Imperial is re-attested as a member from 14 Sep 2019 via a member-written Wattpad history, and [[Paladins United]] is first attested a member the same day.{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}}

That memoir, written by [[arkada|Arkada]] of [[titans-valor|Titans Valor]] as the September 2019 fighting was still going on, also states something the chronicle data cannot support: "The Valkyrie alliance, consisting of Kingdom Foxes, Imperial, Paladins United, and Emorians, have existed for longer than I've played Wynncraft."{{cite:wattpad-com-784189853-inside-myself-recent-wynncraft-guild-history|“THE FAILED RAID”, 14 Sep 2019}} The chronicle records Imperial and Paladins United as joining Valkyrie only on 13 Sep 2019, the day before{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}, and Imperial's own departure from the alliance in 2016 is attested in the relaunch thread of that October.{{cite:thread-159734|post #7, Ascended Kitten, 15 Oct 2016}} The discrepancy is best read as a war-time observer describing the bloc he was fighting by its component guilds and assuming their association was as old as the alliance name; the chronicle's join dates record first attestation, not necessarily first association, and the record between 2017 and 2019 is thin enough that a longer, unrecorded Imperial or Paladins United association cannot be excluded. The dates in the data are left unchanged.

### Final years (2020–2022)
Valkyrie still described itself as a community alliance "built on friendship" in 2020{{cite:thread-263975-p04|post #63, Haisay, 9 Mar 2020}}, and a Paladins United member wrote simply "In Valk" in March 2020.{{cite:https://forums.wynncraft.com/threads/135149/|Wynncraft forums thread 135149, Mar 2020 (via Wayback Machine)}} Through the May 2021 realignment that produced [[Valhalla]] and [[Khaos]], a [[the-forum-megalist|forum megalist]] contributor noted that "Valkyrie stayed the same" while the two major alliances renamed.{{cite:thread-278112-p07|post #136, Dream, 25 May 2021}} Paladins United's thread OP listed "Valkyrie and [[Hestia]], both community alliances" from Nov 2021{{cite:thread-246617|opening post, Wayback capture 28 Nov 2021}} until 19 Sep 2022 — the last attestation of Valkyrie anywhere.{{cite:Wayback Machine capture of the Paladins United guild thread, 19 Sep 2022}} No dissolution was ever recorded. The satirical "Greater Valkyrie Alliance" thread of October 2022 involved unrelated guilds trading on the name.

## Membership
Valkyrie's full roster was never published in any era. The largest attested concurrent membership is the four guilds of the August 2016 relaunch — Imperial, Kingdom of Foxes, House of Sentinels and Lightly Toasted Heroes{{cite:thread-147790|post #1, opening post (thread opened 29 Aug 2016)}} — none of which falls inside the machine-recorded chronicle window, which begins in January 2018 and records only three guilds at once.{{cite:Chronicle alliance and event records}}

